{
  "schema": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "overview",
    "description": "Plan-driven development for Claude Code - the model, the modes, and the per-repo footprint"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "id": "overview",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "overview"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "plankit preserves approved Claude Code plans, guards protected branches, and derives releases from commit messages. It ships as a Claude Code plugin. These skills are the documentation; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " renders the same pages in a terminal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "model",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Model"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Claude plans the work. On approval, the preserve hook copies the plan, byte for byte, into the plans directory under a dated, sequenced filename. The protect hook denies edits there. The guard hook denies or questions git mutations on protected branches."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "per-repo-footprint",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Per-repo footprint"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A configured repository carries "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the committed policy: modes, protected branches, changelog sections, release hooks. Those commands run through "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "sh -c"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", or "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "cmd /c"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " on Windows. Its "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".claude/settings.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " carries the plankit marketplace under "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "extraKnownMarketplaces"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "plankit@plankit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " under "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "enabledPlugins"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", so a teammate who trusts the folder has the marketplace and is one "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "/plugin install"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " from the plugin; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk status"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " spells out any entry that is missing. The plans directory appears when the first plan is preserved. Without "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", every hook exits without acting."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "commit-conventions",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Commit conventions"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Work commits follow Conventional Commits: "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "type(scope): subject"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " after the type or a "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "BREAKING CHANGE:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " footer marks a breaking change. The type table is "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "changelog.types"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " in "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk init"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " writes the default table, listed under "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help changelog"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk changelog --dry-run"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " previews how the current commits will land. Never add a breaking marker on your own judgment; see "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help guard"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", Breaking markers. The commits decide the version; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--bump"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " on the release commands is the developer's, see "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help ship"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", Deciding the version."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "commands",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Commands"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " prints the topic index. Each command's page is also a "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "/plankit:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " shortcut in Claude Code."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "updating",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Updating"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "/plugin marketplace update plankit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", then "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "/plugin update plankit@plankit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", then "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "/reload-plugins"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". A new release changes the plugin only; no repository changes. A pk installed with "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "go install"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " or Homebrew is updated separately, and the brief says when it is behind the plugin."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "cloud-sessions",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Cloud sessions"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A cloud session at claude.ai/code starts from a fresh clone and never installs the plugins a repository enables, so plankit's hooks and skills are absent there unless the cloud environment installs the plugin. Give the environment a setup script:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "text": "#!/bin/bash\nset -x\nif command -v claude \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then\n  claude plugin install plankit --marketplace https://plankit.com/marketplace.json --scope user \\\n    || echo \"setup: plankit install failed\" \u003e\u00262\nelse\n  echo \"setup: claude CLI not on PATH during setup\" \u003e\u00262\nfi\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every line is non-fatal: a non-zero exit stops the session starting. Under Network access, allow "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "plankit.com"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "github.com"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "*.githubusercontent.com"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "; the plugin archive is a GitHub release asset and downloads through a redirect to the last of those. The environment is set once per account, in the environment selector under the message box, and serves every repository that enables the plugin."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To confirm it took effect, ask a session in that environment to run "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk status"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ": pk is only present when the plugin installed, so the policy block printing is the proof. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk: command not found"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " means the session is in an environment without the script; pick the right environment rather than installing pk by hand, which gives a session pk without the hooks. Tags are not part of the clone; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk changelog"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " fetches them from origin when none are present."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "migrating-from-pre-plugin-plankit-v0-x",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Migrating from pre-plugin plankit (v0.x)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The plugin replaces the files "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk setup"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " copied into a repository. In a repository configured by a v0.x release:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "para",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Remove the plankit hook entries (guard, protect, preserve, and the install-pk SessionStart entry) from "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": ".claude/settings.json"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". The plugin wires the same hooks, and leftover entries fire twice."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "para",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Delete "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": ".claude/install-pk.sh"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", the copied "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": ".claude/skills/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", and "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": ".claude/rules/plankit/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "para",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Keep "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": ".pk.json"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and the plans directory. The config schema is unchanged."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "windows-without-git-bash",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Windows without Git Bash"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When Git for Windows is absent, Claude Code's shell tool is PowerShell, and the plugin's "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "bin/"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " directory is not on its PATH. Invoke pk by its full path:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "text": "\u0026 \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\\bin\\pk.cmd\" status\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Claude Code substitutes "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when it loads this page. In a terminal, "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " shows the placeholder verbatim."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
